Unit tests (no ESP32 or network connection required)
===================================================

Run from the project root:
    python test/run_tests.py

Requirements:
- Python 3
- Node.js 18+
- g++ / clang++ on PATH, or a local Zig C++ compiler:
    python -m pip install --target .pio/test-tools ziglang==0.16.0

The runner uses .pio for compiled binaries and compiler caches.
It exits with a nonzero status on compilation errors or failed assertions.
These host tests use a standalone runner, not "pio test".

Coverage:
- Actual MuteTimer.h used by main.cpp: idle state, 30-second pause,
  ceiling of remaining seconds, expiry boundary, repeated requests,
  reactivation and uint32_t millis() overflow.
- Actual data/index.js in an isolated mock DOM: lamp and buzzer states,
  countdown, lamp off during mute, POST /mute, request failures,
  lost connection and recovery, notification text/age, uptime formatting,
  polling and request timeout cleanup.

Commands for individual suites:
    node --test test/unit/dashboard.test.cjs
    (The C++ suite is compiled and run by test/run_tests.py.)

Firmware compile check:
    pio run -e esp32dev

Limitations:
These tests do not exercise physical GPIO, button interrupts, FreeRTOS
scheduling, Wi-Fi, SPIFFS or real ntfy delivery. The dashboard uses fake
HTTP replies; HTTP routes and rendering in a real browser are not covered.
Verify these separately on the ESP32. Tests do not flash the board or send
notifications.

MuteButton coverage: short pulses, held input at startup, stable press/release, release bounce and millis overflow. Physical button is polled; hold for at least 100 ms for reliable detection with the 20 ms loop interval.
